title "End User Desktop and SaaS Software (Fly)"
layout tiers

# not modelled: Domains legend, relationship-style legend,
#   footnote "** TBD by your business naming structure of your services"
#   (the ** markers on Business Service names are dropped)

BC manage-tech: Manage Technology
BC create-docs: Create Documentation
BC create-content: Create Content
BC conduct-research: Conduct Research
BC communicate: Communicate and Collaborate
BC manage-finances: Manage Finances
BC manage-hr: Manage Human Resources

CI(Computer) users-computer: User's Computer

BSO acrobat: Adobe Acrobat
BSO ms-office: Microsoft Office - Std
BSO chrome: Google Chrome
BSO teams: Teams
# * on the slide marks the SaaS offerings (accessed from rather than installed on the computer)
BSO clockify: Clockify Time Tracker
BSO monitask: Monitask Desktop Monitoring

BS client-computing: Client Computing
BS doc-content: Documentation and Content Services (TBD)
BS desktop-software: Desktop Software Services (TBD)
BS direct-messaging: Direct Messaging Services (TBD)
BS payroll: Payroll Services (TBD)
BS employee-mgmt: Employee Mgmt Services (TBD)

SP technology-service: Technology Service
SP end-user: End User Services
SP financial: Financial Services Portfolio
SP hr-services: Human Resource Services

# Strategic (Provided by::Provides). Create Documentation has no line of its own:
# the purple connector starting at Create Content runs behind Create
# Documentation and Adobe Acrobat down to Documentation and Content Services.
manage-tech -> client-computing
create-content -> doc-content
conduct-research -> desktop-software
communicate -> direct-messaging
manage-finances -> payroll
manage-hr -> employee-mgmt

# The slide draws a dashed References arrow from the CI box to Client Computing
# (not a CSDM pair; kept as shown).
users-computer -> client-computing : References
acrobat -> doc-content
ms-office -> doc-content
chrome -> desktop-software
teams -> direct-messaging
clockify -> payroll
monitask -> employee-mgmt

# One dotted arrow runs from Monitask straight through every offering into the
# CI, labelled "*Installed on / *Accessed from"; read as each offering -> CI.
acrobat -> users-computer : Installed on / Accessed from
ms-office -> users-computer : Installed on / Accessed from
chrome -> users-computer : Installed on / Accessed from
teams -> users-computer : Installed on / Accessed from
clockify -> users-computer : Installed on / Accessed from
monitask -> users-computer : Installed on / Accessed from

client-computing -> technology-service
doc-content -> end-user
desktop-software -> end-user
# Desktop Software Services also has a dotted reference to the Technology Service portfolio.
desktop-software -> technology-service
direct-messaging -> end-user
payroll -> financial
employee-mgmt -> hr-services
